<title>RUSSIA: Russia sows more wheat by June 9, less maize, beet.</title>
<headline>Russia sows more wheat by June 9, less maize, beet.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's spring sowing campaign is drawing to a close, with slightly more land sown to wheat by June 9 from year-ago levels but significantly less to maize and sugar beet, the State Statistics Committee said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said wheat sowings were three percent above year-ago levels, while maize was down 15 percent and sugar beets 20 percent lower.</p>
<p>The total area sown so far to spring grains, excluding maize, was 35.12 million hectares, up 0.1 percent from year-ago levels.</p>
<p>The committee released the following data--</p>
<p>	     RUSSIAN 1997 SPRING SOWING CAMPAIGN AS OF JUNE 9</p>
<p>			 AREA SOWN (1,000 hectares)</p>
<p>				 June 9, 1997	pct change from</p>
<p>							 year-ago level</p>
<p> All spring crops	     52,333	     -5.0</p>
<p>  grains (not incl maize)   35,117	     +0.1</p>
<p>  wheat			   14,917	     +3.0</p>
<p>  all maize			5,302	    -15.0</p>
<p>  food maize			 598	    -16.0</p>
